Function: ref_enso_h_W_filter
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_h_W_unobs.m
Lines: 1194-1252
Inputs: T_C, T_E, I, h_W, L_x, L_y, f_x, f_y, S_x, sigma_C, sigma_h, N, dt
Outputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, S_xoS_x_inv, S_yoS_y
ConsumedOnly: h_W=1
Pairs: aci_filter, aci_conditional
Note: The one ENSO configuration that ships with CONDITIONAL ACI enabled, and
 the reason this record's input list could not be taken from the shared
 template. Line 1202, `S_xoS_x_inv(1, 1, :) = 1/sigma_C^2;`, carries leading
 whitespace rather than a comment marker and is live, so the block consumes
 `sigma_C` -- a name no other ENSO filter block mentions -- and the extract
 will not call without it. `sigma_h` is the second such name, consumed at line
 1211 to form the latent-noise Grammian, which the vector configuration takes
 from a matrix instead.
 .
 What that live line does is the conditional analysis itself. The
 pseudoinverse at line 1197 fills slice one, line 1202 then overwrites the
 (1,1) entry across every slice, and the per-step pinv at line 1251 is
 commented out as the script's own instructions direct -- so from step two the
 observation-noise inverse is diag(1/sigma_C^2, 0, 0) and only the T_C channel
 informs the latent state. This computes h_W(t) -> T_C | (u, T_E, tau, I),
 where the other four scripts compute an unconditional ACI. `S_x` is therefore
 consumed at slice one alone.
 .
 The latent state is a scalar against a three-dimensional observation, which
 is the configuration the profile's `size(filter_mean, 1) == 1` discriminator
 asserts.

Function: ref_enso_h_W_smoother
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_h_W_unobs.m
Lines: 1258-1318
Inputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, L_x, L_y, f_y, S_yoS_y, S_xoS_x_inv, N, dt
Outputs: smoother_mean, smoother_cov, E_j_matrices, F_j_matrices
Pairs: aci_smoother, .aci_online_aux
Note: Backward smoother and online-smoother auxiliaries for the h_W
 configuration, in one loop as elsewhere. It consumes no observation at all --
 the model carries no noise cross-interaction terms, so the backward mean
 update is driven by the filter statistics and `f_y` alone and never forms an
 observation increment. That is why the earlier attempt to derive its inputs
 from the vector template failed in the other direction from the filter's: it
 was handed T_C, T_E and I, which this range does not use.
 .
 `F_j_matrices` is 1 x 3 x (N+1) here rather than scalar, the latent state
 being one-dimensional and the observation three-dimensional.

Function: ref_enso_T_C_filter
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_T_C_unobs.m
Lines: 1201-1257
Inputs: T_C, T_E, I, L_x, L_y, f_x, f_y, S_x, sigma_C, sigma_E, N, dt
Outputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, S_xoS_x_inv, S_yoS_y
ConsumedOnly: T_C=1
Pairs: aci_filter, aci_conditional
Note: The configuration in which T_C alone is unobserved. Its observation is
 TWO-dimensional, (T_E, I), so S_xoS_x_inv is 2x2 where the other four scripts
 make it 3x3 -- and `L_y` is per-step here while `L_x` is constant, the mirror
 of the tau and u cases. Both are reasons this input list could not be taken
 from a shared template.
 .
 Line 1209, `S_xoS_x_inv(1, 1, :) = 1/sigma_E^2;`, is LIVE -- in column one,
 with no comment marker -- and the per-step pinv at line 1255 is commented out.
 This script therefore computes the CONDITIONAL quantity
 T_C(t) -> T_E | (u, h_W, tau, I), not the unconditional ACI. See the
 correction to F7 in the parity report; the earlier reading of this file was
 wrong.

Function: ref_enso_T_C_smoother
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_T_C_unobs.m
Lines: 1263-1323
Inputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, L_x, L_y, f_y, S_yoS_y, S_xoS_x_inv, N, dt
Outputs: smoother_mean, smoother_cov, E_j_matrices, F_j_matrices
Pairs: aci_smoother, .aci_online_aux
Note: Backward smoother and online-smoother auxiliaries for the T_C
 configuration. It consumes no observation: this model carries no noise
 cross-interaction terms, so the backward mean update is driven by the filter
 statistics and `f_y` alone. `F_j_matrices` is 1 x 2 x (N+1), the observation
 being two-dimensional here.

Function: ref_enso_tau_filter
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_tau_unobs.m
Lines: 1197-1255
Inputs: T_C, T_E, I, tau, L_x, L_y, f_x, f_y, S_x, S_y, N, dt
Outputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, S_xoS_x_inv, S_yoS_y
ConsumedOnly: tau=1
Pairs: aci_filter
Note: The configuration in which tau alone is unobserved. This one takes `S_y`
 rather than a sigma scalar, because it forms the latent-noise Grammian as
 `S_y.^2` from a time-varying feedback -- a third distinct shape for the same
 quantity across five scripts, and the reason the shared template could not
 supply it.
 .
 Every conditional-ACI line here is commented and the per-step pinv at line
 1253 is live, so this script computes the UNCONDITIONAL ACI. Its guidance
 comments are nonetheless copied verbatim from the h_W script and still name
 h_W as the latent variable; that is a documentation defect in the reference,
 not a computational one.

Function: ref_enso_tau_smoother
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_tau_unobs.m
Lines: 1261-1321
Inputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, L_x, L_y, f_y, S_yoS_y, S_xoS_x_inv, N, dt
Outputs: smoother_mean, smoother_cov, E_j_matrices, F_j_matrices
Pairs: aci_smoother, .aci_online_aux
Note: Backward smoother and online-smoother auxiliaries for the tau
 configuration, with `L_x` per-step as in its filter.

Function: ref_enso_u_filter
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_u_unobs.m
Lines: 1197-1255
Inputs: T_C, T_E, I, u, L_x, L_y, f_x, f_y, S_x, sigma_C, sigma_u, N, dt
Outputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, S_xoS_x_inv, S_yoS_y
ConsumedOnly: u=1
Pairs: aci_filter, aci_conditional
Note: The configuration in which u alone is unobserved. Line 1205,
 `S_xoS_x_inv(1, 1, :) = 1/sigma_C^2;`, is LIVE -- in column one, with no
 comment marker -- and the per-step pinv at line 1253 is commented out, so
 this script computes the CONDITIONAL quantity u(t) -> T_C | (h_W, T_E, tau, I).
 See the correction to F7 in the parity report.
 .
 `sigma_u` is the name that distinguishes this input list: the latent-noise
 Grammian is `sigma_u^2` here, where h_W uses `sigma_h`, T_C uses `sigma_C`
 and tau uses a time-varying `S_y`.

Function: ref_enso_u_smoother
Script: ENSO_model_cond_ACI_u_unobs.m
Lines: 1261-1321
Inputs: filter_mean, filter_cov, L_x, L_y, f_y, S_yoS_y, S_xoS_x_inv, N, dt
Outputs: smoother_mean, smoother_cov, E_j_matrices, F_j_matrices
Pairs: aci_smoother, .aci_online_aux
Note: Backward smoother and online-smoother auxiliaries for the u
 configuration, with `L_x` per-step as in its filter.
